  <h2>Which one should you pick</h2>

  <p><strong>TalkPal</strong> is the better choice if your language isn't one of Vocele's nine, you want to practice on Android or a laptop, you like switching between roleplays, debates and characters, or you want to talk a little every day for free.</p>

  <p><strong>Vocele</strong> is the better choice if you understand far more than you can say and <a href="/blog/understand-english-but-cant-speak">freeze when it's your turn</a>, you want the words from today's conversation to still be there next month, or you want to see a specific sound improve in numbers rather than colors.</p>

  <p>If avatars and a big lesson library matter more, read <a href="/vs/praktika">Vocele vs Praktika</a>. If your English problem lives in work meetings, <a href="/vs/fluently">Vocele vs Fluently</a> covers the professional coaches. And if you're really weighing an app against a human tutor at $200 to $320 a month, <a href="/blog/ai-speaking-coach-vs-human-tutor">the AI coach vs human tutor comparison</a> is honest about where apps lose.</p>

  <p>Vocele isn't on the App Store yet. If the sound-level history or the corrections inside your sentence are what you came for, <a href="/pricing">see the plans and the 3-day trial</a>. I'll update this page when the listing goes live.</p>
